SECTION II: THE PRINCIPLES
GOVERNING MEDIATION

holds preparatory talks with each party with the
goal to:
a) building trust with the parties;
b) to identify participants to attend the
mediation and know if they have powers to
make necessary decisions;
c) to encourage them to come to mediation
and participate fully;
d) to agree with the parties on how long the
process will take and how many sessions;
e) to understand the relationship between the
parties;
f) to address any concerns that both parties
may have;
g) to help both parties to prepare for the
mediation.

